WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.283
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.690
NARRATOR: It's a playground
staple a stationary ride

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.270
on cartoon animal that
bounces up and down

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:13.400
and rocks back and
forth, courtesy

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.000
of a huge spring underneath
secured into the ground.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.130
The bouncy coil
base is what gives

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.780
this type of
playground equipment

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.730
its name, a spring rider.

00:00:24.188 --> 00:00:26.620
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.650
The spring rider is a
playground favorite.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.380
To withstand years of
rambunctious riders,

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.960
it has to be solid and durable.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.870
Yet, for a toddler to be
able to rock back and forth,

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.640
it can't be too heavy.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.270
That's why this spring is made
of thick steel and the animal,

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.912
of lightweight aluminum.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.650
That sand core is
comprised of halves,

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.900
each made with an
aluminum mold--

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.700
duck-shaped, in this case.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.670
Workers fill it with
sand and adhesive mix

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.220
that sets into a solid block.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.240
They insert several
steel support rods,

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.680
fill to the top, and
even out the surface,

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.690
then expose two
hooks they'll later

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.780
grab to extract the
core half, once the sand

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.640
hardens in about 20 minutes.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.000
Meanwhile, other
workers use an aluminum

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.750
pattern to make each half
of the duck casting mold.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.650
After applying a powder release
agent to prevent sticky,

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.960
they cover the pattern
with a sieved mixture

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.070
of sand and clay.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.280
They mount a frame
around the pattern

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.910
to contain the sand as
they add more and more,

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.340
repeatedly packing
it down in all areas

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:40.910
with a pneumatic ramming tool.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.090
Then they remove
the frame and cover

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:47.830
the sand with a wooden board.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.470
This provides a hard
surface for the press,

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:53.735
which now applies the weight
of about four midsize SUVs.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:58.540
Then they flip over the
mold and remove the pattern

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.490
which formed the mold cavity.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:03.220
The sand is now so
firmly compacted

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.440
that it holds the shape.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.020
One half of the sand
mold has channels,

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.740
through which the molten metal
will flow into the cavity.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:14.620
Workers now position
several 1/4 inch thick foam

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:19.160
spacers in the cavity and place
1/2 of the core on top of them.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.300
The spacers elevate the
core, creating a 1/4 inch

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.145
cavity between core and mold.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.820
The other half of
the core goes on top.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:33.520
After placing spacers on top
of that to create a 1/4 inch

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.400
gap on this side as well,
they carefully lowered

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.860
the other half of the sand.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:42.040
Now they're ready
to cast the duck.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.020
The melting point
of aluminum is just

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.690
over 1,090 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:50.540
However, they heat much
higher to 1,400 degrees

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.980
so it'll flow faster and
fill the entire cavity

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.840
before beginning to solidify.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.350
They pour the metal
through holes on top.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.360
It flows through the
runners into the mold

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.450
cavity, which is that
1/4 inch gap surrounding

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.790
the duck-shaped core.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:09.100
About 20 minutes
later, the metal

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.680
has cooled and solidified.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.590
They break the mold apart
on a vibrating sieve,

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.900
releasing the aluminum
duck and shaking

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:20.560
out the core sand through a
hole at the bottom of the duck.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.140
After cutting off excess
aluminum that hardened

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.990
in the runners, they
grind down the seam,

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.465
which formed in between
the two halves of the mold.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:34.150
Next, they weld on aluminum
handles for the child to grip

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.680
when riding.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.740
These handles are cast in
sand molds just like the duck.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.860
Workers grind down the
weld and any sharp edges,

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:47.120
making the entire
surface nice and smooth.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.508
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:59.650
Next, a coat of polyester powder
in bright, rubber ducky yellow,

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:03.310
then a 20 minute trip through
an oven to bake the coating,

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:04.570
making it ultra durable.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:09.550
Now delicately airbrushed
with the urethane

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:13.840
enamel paint, the details
that bring Mr. Duck to life--

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.569
his feet, wings, bill, and eyes.

00:04:18.769 --> 00:04:21.230
The thick coil that
makes this a spring rider

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:23.195
is made of a flexible
type of steel.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:30.510
They bolt a steel
spacer play to it

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.850
then hide the bolts
under an aluminum cover.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.640
After attaching a
footrest-- steel again--

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.140
they bolt the duck to the plate.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:47.010
All these parts, like the duck,
are painted with baked on,

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.090
polyester coating.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.640
The spring bolts to a concrete
block buried under ground.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.130
Ducky and friends are
designed to withstand even

00:04:56.130 --> 00:05:00.030
the harshest winters, letting
children enjoy a little spring

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:00.870
all year-round.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:04.220
[MUSIC PLAYING]

